From 9642ab74edd14455f15bff7dd002e737c1af225b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:05:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): a slow annotation refresh no longer holds the
 session read that started it [daveey]

GET /api/sessions/<id> on hermes-hub found the annotation refresh lock free and ran the whole
read (counts, remote-links projection, waiting sources) on its own worker. Inside a Desktop poll
burst (15 concurrent session-list reads) that took 5.348 s and the Desktop's 5 s timeout fired
(2026-10-31 23:33:12 UTC, t_01a19451dffa47a8). A poll with a previous read of its scope now runs
the refresh on a helper thread, waits at most _REFRESH_WAIT_S (1 s) for it, and otherwise serves
the previous read dated by its read time; a cold scope still reads inline. Fast reads keep
read-your-writes and raise their own errors.
